// Generators (after ACEP_PSIL and IEEE9500): model 1 by pf, by kvar and by the default pf 0.88 (and kVA 1.2 x kW);
// delta; kW=0 with pf=0.98 and kvar=0 (they agree); model 7 (current-limited, as model 1); model 3 (a PV bus,
// after SteamGen1) with Vpu; a 1-phase machine (ratedU x sqrt 3).
Clear
New Circuit.atom basekv=4.16 bus1=sourcebus pu=1.0 MVAsc3=20000 MVAsc1=21000
New Line.l1 bus1=sourcebus bus2=b1 phases=3 r1=0.1 x1=0.2 r0=0.3 x0=0.6 length=1 units=kft
New Transformer.t phases=3 buses=[b1 b2] kVs=[4.16 0.48] kVAs=[2000 2000] xhl=5
New Generator.pq bus1=b2 kv=0.48 kW=100 pf=0.95 kVA=250 Xdp=0.27 Xdpp=0.2 H=2
New Generator.delta bus1=b2 kv=0.48 kW=50 kVA=250 conn=delta pf=0.98
New Generator.vars bus1=b2 kv=0.48 kW=20 kvar=5 kVA=75
New Generator.plain bus1=b2 kv=0.48 kW=100
New Generator.idle bus1=b2 kv=0.48 kW=0 kVA=250 conn=delta pf=0.98 kvar=0
New Generator.limited bus1=b2 kv=0.48 kW=0 kvar=30 model=7 kVA=775
New Generator.steam bus1=b1 kV=4.16 kW=1000 kVA=4000 model=3 Vpu=1.02
New Generator.single bus1=b2.1 phases=1 kv=0.277 kW=10 pf=0.95 kVA=12
